senses.gloss:
yogācāra, m.,
(1) (AMg. jogāyāra; rare in Skt., not in Pali, where yogāvacara seems to correspond), practice of spiritual discipline: Mvy 〔1638〕; Śikṣ 〔55.17〕 (˚cāra-bhūmyanukūlāni khādanīya-bhojanīyāni);
(2) as Bhvr., = ˚cārin, one who is characterized by yogācāra (1): ˚cāro (or read ˚cārī?) bhikṣur KP 〔108.4〕;
(3) n. of a samādhi: Kv 〔83.10〕;
(4) pl., adherents of the Buddhist school of this name; social relations with them cause or constitute backsliding for Bodhisattvas: Mv 〔i.120.9〕. Cf. foll. items.
